-- title:
--   Sections determined by their image under `Proj.map` of φ
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring and $K$ a field (in the same universe), let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $T$, regarded with its projective model, and let $f : T \to K$ be a ring homomorphism, so that $W.\mathrm{map}\ f$ is the Weierstrass curve over $K$ obtained by applying $f$ to the coefficients. For a Weierstrass curve $V$ over a ring $R$, `projModelGradingCR V` is the grading on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\ 3, R)$ modulo the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $V$ given by pushing the standard homogeneous submodules forward along the quotient map, and `projModelStrCR V` is the structure morphism from $\mathrm{Proj}$ of that grading to $\mathrm{Spec}\ R$ (the canonical map to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the degree-zero part, followed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $R \to (\text{degree }0)$). Let $\varphi$ be a homomorphism of graded rings from `projModelGradingCR W` to `projModelGradingCR (W.map f)` such that the irrelevant ideal of the target is contained in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source (the hypothesis making $\mathrm{Proj}.\mathrm{map}\ \varphi$ defined), and assume `IsCoefficientHom W f φ`, i.e. $\varphi$ carries the class of a constant $C\,a$ to the class of $C\,(f a)$ for every $a \in T$ and the class of $X_i$ to the class of $X_i$ for each $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ 3$. Let $s_1, s_2$ be sections of the projective model of $W.\mathrm{map}\ f$, that is, morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}\ K \to \mathrm{Proj}(\mathtt{projModelGradingCR}\,(W.\mathrm{map}\ f))$ whose composite with `projModelStrCR (W.map f)` is the identity of $\mathrm{Spec}\ K$. If the composites of the underlying morphisms of $s_1$ and $s_2$ with $\mathrm{Proj}.\mathrm{map}\ \varphi$ agree, then $s_1 = s_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the statement that $K$-points of the projective model of the base-changed Weierstrass curve are the same thing as $K$-points of the projective model of $W$ lying over the given homomorphism $f$ of base rings; it expresses that the comparison morphism induced on $\mathrm{Proj}$ by a coefficient homomorphism is injective on sections over the base. It is used in the construction of level structures and Drinfeld bases on Weierstrass models, where points of a base-changed model have to be identified with points of the original one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_DrinfeldGlobal_section_eq_of_comp_projMap_eq_of_isCoefficientHom.lean

